  "verdict": {
    "coexistence_on_non_shared": "FAIL",
    "detail": "With the read worker holding a non-shared project (lock PID = the read worker's own interpreter), a second process's OpenProject(writeEnabled=True) raises FP_FileLockedError ('This project is in use by another program'). The same open succeeds once the read worker is released. The two opens cannot coexist; FR-027's 'try_word answers during filing' cannot hold on a non-shared project.",
    "m1_outcome": "M-1 interim restriction STAYS (reads refused during filing on non-shared projects; the read worker is released before the writable open, now unconditionally on non-shared). Per T005, stop as needs_human for a maintainer amendment of FR-027.",
    "filing_on_production_path": "completed, persisted: 1 word filed (reapproved 1, deleted 0 against a projected upper bound of 1); the .fwdata changed; a fresh read worker re-reads the parser-evaluated analysis afterwards",
    "read_worker_release_rewrites_file": false,
    "xample_refusal_path_rewrites_file": false,
    "xample_note": "The memory-noted save (parse-worker-saves-xample-project) was NOT reproduced on the try_word engine-refusal path: the Sena 3 copy's sha256 and mtime are unchanged after the refused open and the release. Its root cause lies on a path that gets further than the engine gate (the original test_parse_live run).",
    "defects_found_and_fixed_on_the_way": [
      "parser_probe: Assembly.LoadFile did not resolve ParserCore's dependencies in a process that had not imported flexicon, so filing's preflight refused parser_core_missing on a healthy install (and the read-spine probe had the same latent failure); fixed with an AssemblyResolve handler over ParserCore's own folder",
      "handlers/parse: the access gate refused the server's OWN read worker's lock as held_by_other; now recognised (worker reports its own pid in 'ready'; a venv launcher's pid is not the lock holder) and released before re-probing",
      "filing worker: flexicon's HeadlessLcmUI.SynchronizeInvoke is None; HCParser's ParserModelChangeListener subscribes to change notifications, so FieldWorks' filer died with NullReferenceException in SendPropChangedNotifications; fixed with a HeadlessLcmUI subclass returning SIL.LCModel.Utils.SingleThreadedSynchronizeInvoke",
      "runner: a filing run that stopped on an error and then saved recorded error=null; the cause is now recorded"
    ]
